@ 37.2 - Proto-Siouan-Iroquoian to Proto-Siouan
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Chafe, Wallace L. (1964), “Another Look at Siouan and Iroquoian”. American Anthropologist New Series, 66:852 – 862; and from cedh aumdmanh’s Iroquoian changes
	ẽ õ → ı̃ ũ
	{t,h} → ∅ / s_
	h → ∅ / V_C
	s → ∅ / h_
	θ → r
	ʔ → ∅ / V_
	x → ç / _{i,u}
	# Also, apparently /tʲ/ got picked up and added to the phonology somewhere along the line, but the circumstances are unclear